It isn't hung. The probe is running three of the distance checks at once, started at 05:55 UTC and now about 11 minutes in:
- the library as it is today;
- the checker with its filter lifted, which shows where the library uses the pattern;
- a prototype of Scala's way.

Each Java process is using a full CPU. One such check takes about 15 minutes alone on an idle machine. Three at once take longer, so I expect them done around 06:15 to 06:25 UTC. The worker checks on them every 4.5 minutes and last wrote at 06:03.

It has already done the rest:
- a prototype of Scala's way under walk, which ran B's body for calls through both A and B;
- small test programs on both paths;
- a comparison with real Scala. Scala refuses an object that gets two bodies from two traits unless it declares its own.

It has written 0.54M so far, past its 0.5M estimate. It's close to done, so I'm letting it finish.

The git-check hook has been back on since a VM restart at 04:16 UTC. The next process stop is due around 17:16 UTC (19:16 your time). The check-in for it is moved there.

